    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Zurich Zebras centers on maximizing stolen base potential and leveraging favorable matchups against high-xERA starting pitching. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leads the charge with an elite 80.98 score, as his spot at the top of the lineup combined with a favorable matchup against Kyle Leahy allows him to capitalize on his elite speed. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (75.84) stands out as a prime play against Merrill Kelly; despite a mediocre BvP history, his platoon advantage and expected run-scoring environment make him a core anchor for the day. While **Trea Turner** (68.32) and **Kyle Schwarber** (67.57) provide significant upside, both face a 42% rain risk, which injects a layer of volatility into their expected production. **Colt Keith** (63.76) and **Caleb Durbin** (63.89) provide high-floor contributions, with **Caleb Durbin** specifically targeted for his ability to navigate a weak matchup against Sam Aldegheri.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Luke Raley**, whose score of 59.03 fell just short of our starting threshold. While **Luke Raley** benefited from a favorable matchup against Shane Bieber, the optimizer favored the higher overall output and strategic slotting of **Junior Caminero** (62.30) and **Casey Schmitt** (62.28). **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.64) remains in the lineup despite a lower score, as his utility as a 3B anchor carries more weight in our current roster construction than forcing a bench-heavy approach. Investors should monitor the lineup status for **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Trea Turner**, **Christian Yelich**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Junior Caminero** closely; as their final batting order positions are not yet confirmed, any shift toward the bottom of the order will adjust their daily efficiency scores, though they remain the most efficient options currently available to the Zurich Zebras.",
